## Can foreigners buy here?

Yes. Like everywhere in Mauritius, foreigners can buy in Chamarel through the schemes managed by the Economic Development Board: the [PDS](/en/living-in-the-west/pds), [IRS](/en/living-in-the-west/irs), [RES](/en/living-in-the-west/res) and [Smart City](/en/living-in-the-west/smart-city) schemes, or by buying an apartment of at least MUR 6 million in a building with at least two floors above the ground floor. A home of **USD 375,000 or more** comes with a residence permit for as long as you own it.

## What the official lists show

One project on the EDB's November 2022 list of Real Estate Scheme projects is in Chamarel. There is no smart city in Chamarel; the nearest is Cap Tamarin. The RES list dates from 2022, and the EDB does not publish a full list of PDS projects on its website, so ask any developer for its current scheme certificate.

## Costs on top of the price

- Registration duty: 5% of the price under the PDS; under the IRS and RES, USD 70,000 or 5% on a first purchase, whichever is lower.
- The EDB's processing fee: MUR 25,000 per application.
- Notary fees: ask for a written quote.

The full process, from reservation to residence permit, is in [how buying works](/en/living-in-the-west/how-buying-works).

## Living in Chamarel

Port Louis is about 45 km away by car, roughly 54 minutes with no traffic. Schools, clinics, costs and daily life are covered in [Living in Chamarel](/en/areas/chamarel#living).

*Figures come from the official sources listed below, checked on 3 October 2026. Prices change: ask local agents, schools and your notary for current figures before you decide.*
